id: pm-jev-0w3q
title: "pm-jev: typed local-first System One decisions for pm items"
description: "Build pm-jev v0: an opt-in pm extension and library that runs Jev-style System One decision models (local Ollama tev1 by default) over minimized pm item state, returning typed proposals that never mutate items unless --apply clears a configured threshold."
type: Epic
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: agents,"pkg:pm-jev",typesafe-ai
created_at: "2026-10-05T04:38:37.202Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-05T04:39:12.054Z"
assignee: pi-glm
claim_principal: pi-glm
author: pi-glm
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T04:38:56.018Z",pi-glm,"Starting v0 implementation. Orientation verified: local Ollama 0.35.1 serves POST /v1/systemone wire-compatible with the hosted Jev API; @typesafe-ai/sdk 0.6.0 systemOne works against it (~12s per batched call), while the SDK models.list() fails against Ollama ('expected { models: [...] }') so pm-jev models/doctor will fall back to Ollama /api/tags filtered on capability decision. Companion spec: pm-cli-website-flnt (fleet hub)."
tests[1]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
  "npm run test:live",project,pi-glm,"2026-10-05T04:39:12.030Z",local_mutation,feat/typed-local-decisions
body: "Companion spec item: pm-cli-website-flnt (TypeSafe AI Jev integration contract) in the fleet hub; research snapshot docs/pm-jev-typesafe-research-2026-09-26.md. Scope for v0: commands jev triage/dedupe/ask/gate/models/doctor, provider config (local Ollama default, hosted TypeSafe behind an explicit privacy opt-in), full test coverage and fleet CI. Out of scope: Rust client, hosted live acceptance, threshold calibration dataset."
